<title>MALI: Impoverished Mali plugs into the Internet.</title>
<headline>Impoverished Mali plugs into the Internet.</headline>
<dateline>BAMAKO 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The West African state of Mali, one of the world's poorest countries, has plugged into the Internet with help from the United Nations and former colonial power France.</p>
<p>Cottage Industry and Tourism Minister Fatou Haidara presided over the link-up on Thursday. Malian Web surfers will use servers at France's Overseas Scientific and Technical Research Office ORSTOM in Montpelier and the U.N. Development Programme in New York.</p>
</text>
